                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60fb3c25-8057-43aa-be15-fccb4b31b4e7",
                        "source_entry_id": "cbe09372-3650-3245-87a6-6aa6a75de1bf",
                        "source_sense_id": "854db554-f3cc-389e-aca3-a55406a0029f",
                        "target_lang_word": "climax",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "climax",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0efcd30c-abd2-39cc-977a-957399d98ea7",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rhetorical device in which a series is arranged in ascending order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72235e68-cb1b-4b1e-8755-abc91801949e",
                                                "sense_id": "0efcd30c-abd2-39cc-977a-957399d98ea7",
                                                "text": "Ye haue a figure which as well by his Greeke and Latine originals […] may be called the marching figure […] and goeth as it were by ſtrides or paces; it may aſwell by called the clyming figure, for Clymax is as much to ſay as a ladder,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03b8ceec-0bef-4191-98c2-c54a07a5ebc5",
                                                "sense_id": "0efcd30c-abd2-39cc-977a-957399d98ea7",
                                                "text": "Climax, by steps advancing, onward goes\nHigher and still more high to an impassion'd close."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c61be3ac-f2fb-32d9-917d-c46033e6874c",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of such an ascending series."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2711bf76-6aaa-465a-a828-63f9c3f90e6c",
                                                "sense_id": "c61be3ac-f2fb-32d9-917d-c46033e6874c",
                                                "text": "[…]Expressions for the whole Climax of sensibility[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56cb8f6d-1f83-4469-8317-b672bda86529",
                                                "sense_id": "c61be3ac-f2fb-32d9-917d-c46033e6874c",
                                                "text": "The Begums' ministers, on the contrary, to extort from them the disclosure of the place which concealed the treasures, were, […] after being fettered and imprisoned, led out on to a scaffold, and this array of terrours proving unavailing, the meek tempered Middleton, as a dernier resort, menaced them with a confinement in the fortress of Chunargar. Thus, my lords, was a British garrison made the climax of cruelties!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a833b499-21ff-30a3-8e50-b7196ef98e5a",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The culmination of a narrative's rising action, the turning point."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82ce4a30-c994-414b-88ad-d60868e802eb",
                                                "sense_id": "a833b499-21ff-30a3-8e50-b7196ef98e5a",
                                                "text": "As a trafficker in climaxes and thrills and characterization and wonderful dialogue and suspense and confrontations, I had outlined the Dresden story many times."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "973d40d5-c756-309c-9f23-8728462de69f",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A culmination or acme: the last term in an ascending series, particularly"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "often",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c000d2-652b-4964-a06a-69448351007d",
                                                "sense_id": "973d40d5-c756-309c-9f23-8728462de69f",
                                                "text": "In the accomplishment of this, they frequently reach the climax of absurdity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f805b49b-9597-3e61-8ff8-c7452fe817b4",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A culmination or acme: the last term in an ascending series",
                                            "The final term of a rhetorical climax."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "often",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0a73b3e-cc8f-4b59-87ea-3209979bfa7e",
                                                "sense_id": "f805b49b-9597-3e61-8ff8-c7452fe817b4",
                                                "text": "When he adds epithets of praise, his climax is ‘so English’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c90af7d-990f-3e8a-9598-6489a418bbeb",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A culmination or acme: the last term in an ascending series",
                                            "The culmination of ecological development, whereby species are in equilibrium with their environment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "often",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72e9b509-c9cf-4f4f-bef7-2d91f68da4d1",
                                                "sense_id": "4c90af7d-990f-3e8a-9598-6489a418bbeb",
                                                "text": "The succession of associations leading to a climax represents the process of adjustment to the conditions of stress, and the climax represents a condition of relative equilibrium. Climax associations[…] are the resultants of certain climatic, geological[…] conditions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1002d38-b205-38f0-9a18-5d7a21b62143",
                                        "entry_id": "d5ff6910-af17-3f08-9905-a82ee49d5e54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A culmination or acme: the last term in an ascending series",
                                            "The culmination of sexual pleasure, an orgasm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "euphemistic",
                                            "often",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
